  "onboardingTitle": "Before you start",
  "onboardingIntro": "Selene records your cycle on your phone and predicts when your next period is likely to start. We do not collect any of it. The app has no internet permission, and nothing you record leaves your phone unless you choose to send it.",
  "onboardingWhatItIsNotTitle": "What Selene is not",
  "onboardingNotContraception": "Selene is not contraception. It cannot tell you when sex is unlikely to lead to pregnancy, and it must never be used to try.",
  "onboardingNotMedical": "Selene does not give medical advice. If something about your cycle worries you, talk to a doctor or nurse.",
  "onboardingNotDiagnostic": "Predictions come from the dates you record and nothing else, so Selene cannot diagnose anything. Illness, stress, medicines and contraception can all move a period, and predictions do not account for them.",
  "onboardingAlwaysARange": "Predictions come as a range of days, never a single date, because cycles vary too much for one date to be accurate.",
  "onboardingAcknowledge": "I understand",

  "onboardingFirstEntryTitle": "When did your last period start?",
  "onboardingFirstEntryBody": "One date is enough to begin. Predictions start wide and get narrower as you log more cycles.",
  "onboardingFirstEntrySkip": "Skip for now",
  "onboardingFirstEntrySaved": "Saved. You can change it any time.",

