  "privacyHeading": "What this app does with your data",
  "privacyOnDeviceTitle": "We do not collect your information",
  "privacyOnDeviceBody": "The app has no internet permission, no account, no analytics, no advertising and no crash reporting, and a check on every release refuses to build one that asks for the internet. Everything you record stays on your phone, under your control, and none of it reaches us.",
  "privacySharingTitle": "It leaves your phone only when you choose",
  "privacySharingBody": "Two things send anything anywhere, and only when you ask. An export saves a backup file wherever you choose. A web search opens in your browser, after the app tells you exactly which words will be searched, and your browser may keep it in its history.",
  "privacyEncryptedTitle": "The database is encrypted, with a key the phone keeps",
  "privacyEncryptedBody": "Everything you record is kept in the app's private storage, in a database file encrypted with a key held by Android's secure key store. The key never leaves the phone and is not in your exports, so a copy of the file on its own cannot be read. Scheduled reminders are the one exception: until they are due, Android keeps their wording, which can name the predicted dates, outside the encrypted file. Encryption does not protect an unlocked phone. Anyone using it can open the app and read what you recorded unless the app lock is on, and someone with full control of the phone, through root access or a forensic tool, may be able to use the key the way the app does.",
  "privacyBackupTitle": "Nothing is copied off the phone",
  "privacyBackupBody": "Android's cloud backup and device-to-device transfer are switched off for the app, so your records are never copied to a Google account or to a new phone. If you lose the phone, they are gone unless you exported them.",
  "privacyDeletionTitle": "Deleting really deletes",
  "privacyDeletionBody": "You can delete a single day, condition or medicine at any time. Delete everything removes every record and reclaims the space, so the deleted entries are not left readable in the file. Uninstalling the app deletes everything it stored on the phone.",
  "privacyLogsTitle": "The activity log holds nothing you recorded",
  "privacyLogsBody": "The app keeps a short log of what it did, such as \"a prediction was computed\" with a count of cycles. It stays on the phone, only in memory, so it is cleared when the app stops. You can read it and clear it in Settings.",
  "privacyExportTitle": "Exports are yours to look after",
  "privacyExportBody": "An exported backup is a readable file wherever you save it, unless you protect it with a passphrase when you export it. A protected backup opens only with that passphrase, and nobody can recover a forgotten one. Once a backup is saved, it is under your control and the control of wherever you keep or send it.",

  "bootstrapRecoveredTitle": "Your data could not be read",
  "bootstrapRecoveredBody": "The stored file was damaged, so this app started with an empty one. The damaged file is still on the device. If you have a backup, restoring it now is the best way forward.",
  "bootstrapRecoveredAction": "Restore from a backup",
